<% event = @application.event %>
<% founder = @application.user %>

<%# FUIME: the guardian line is about the FOUNDER's own parent or guardian. Under
    merchant-of-record a teen can sell before a parent has done anything and the
    parent gates payouts (Event#payout_setup_blockers), so this is the one place
    to say so plainly. Guarded on `needs_guardian?` — the same predicate that
    blocks the payout — rather than on a pending invite: a founder with no
    guardianship row, or only a revoked one, is exactly as unpaid as one whose
    parent has not clicked yet, and the funnel does not always produce a row
    (spec/models/fuime/selling_without_a_guardian_spec.rb). Which row exists only
    decides whether the fix is "resend" or "invite".

    Under Connect a minor's application cannot activate without an active
    guardian (Event::Application#activation_blockers) unless the school or staff
    exemption applied, so this rarely renders there; when it does, the sentence
    it produces is still true. School ventures are excluded because the school
    stands in for the parent at the payout seam too, and telling a student their
    payout waits on a parent would be false. %>
<% guardian_needed = founder.needs_guardian? && !event.institutionally_sponsored? %>
<% guardian_pending = guardian_needed && founder.guardianships_as_minor.pending.exists? %>

<p>Hey <%= founder.name %>,</p>

<p>
  Welcome to Fuime! You can now log in and open your new business, <%= link_to @application.name, event %>.
  Here's what to do next:
</p>

<%# FUIME: ordered by what gets a founder to a first sale (ONBOARDING_PLAN.md
    §4.1). Upstream led with team invites and account details, neither of which
    is "list something to sell"; those now sit at the bottom. %>
<ul>
  <li>
    <%= link_to "Add what you sell", fuime_offers_url(event_slug: event.slug) %>:
    Name it and price it. Your pay link appears once it's published.
  </li>
  <li>
    <%= link_to "Share your storefront", fuime_storefront_url(slug: event.slug) %>:
    Your storefront is <%= fuime_storefront_url(slug: event.slug) %> — that's where customers see what you sell.
    Paste it in a bio, a group chat or a flyer.
  </li>
  <% if guardian_needed %>
    <li>
      <% if guardian_pending %>
        <strong>Your parent or guardian hasn't signed yet.</strong>
      <% else %>
        <strong>No parent or guardian on your account yet.</strong>
      <% end %>
      <%# "You can sell now" only when it is true. Vetting is a separate admin
          step after activation (Event#operator_vetting_status stays unvetted
          through Event::Application#activate_event!), and the launch scope can
          refuse too, so this reads Event#accepts_payments? rather than the flag.
          Under merchant-of-record the guardian is not among the selling gates
          (Fuime::OperatorEligibility#umbrella_scope_blockers), which is what the
          "don't need" sentence claims and all it claims. %>
      <% if ::Fuime::Features.merchant_of_record? && event.accepts_payments? %>
        You can sell now under Fuime, but nothing is paid out until a guardian accepts.
      <% elsif ::Fuime::Features.merchant_of_record? %>
        You don't need a guardian to start selling, but nothing is paid out until one accepts.
      <% else %>
        Nothing is paid out until a guardian accepts.
      <% end %>
      <% if guardian_pending %>
        <%= link_to "Resend the invite from your Guardian page", guardianships_url %>.
      <% else %>
        <%= link_to "Invite a parent or guardian", new_guardianship_url %>.
      <% end %>
    </li>
  <% end %>
</ul>

<%# FUIME: vetting is the human gate that actually stands between activation and
    a sale (Event#accepts_payments?). Fuime::VettingMailer#approved is the email
    this promises. Shown for `unvetted` only — a rejected or suspended venture is
    not "waiting on us" and should not be told to expect an approval. %>
<% if event.operator_vetting_unvetted? %>
  <p>
    Fuime is reviewing <%= event.name %> by hand — you can set everything up now
    and publish the moment we approve. We'll email you.
  </p>
<% end %>

<%# FUIME-DIVERGENCE: upstream promoted Hack Club's hackathon guide, Discord bot,
    and club toolbox here. Those are Hack Club resources for a nonprofit program
    Fuime does not run, so the tag-specific promo block is removed rather than
    pointed at a Fuime equivalent that does not exist yet. %>

<% if @application.contract&.document.present? %>
  <p>The signed Fuime agreement is available for you to <%= link_to "download here", document_download_url(@application.contract.document) %>.</p>
<% end %>

<%# FUIME: roles in the words the linked page and every role selector use
    (RolesHelper — Owner / Team member / Parent), not the enum's. %>
<p>
  Working with others? <%= link_to "Invite your team", event_team_url(event) %> as <%= role_label("manager").downcase.pluralize %>, <%= role_label("member").downcase.pluralize %>, or a <%= role_label("reader").downcase %> seat — <%= link_to "here's what each role can do", roles_url %>.
  You can also <%= link_to "review your business details", edit_event_url(event) %> any time.
</p>

<p>
  If you would like, you can <%= link_to "schedule an onboarding call", @application.event.onboarding_scheduling_link.presence || event_url(@application.event, request_call: "true") %> with a member of our team,
  or you can contact us at <%= link_to "support@fuime.com", "mailto:support@fuime.com" %> if you have any questions.
</p>

<p>
  Warmly,<br>
  The Fuime team
</p>
